      "rule": "inverse-variance weighted SmoothL1; no censoring treatment",
      "why": "dG_ML is rail-clipped but only ~0.01% of values reach a rail, so there is nothing meaningful to censor. What varies is precision: ~10% of measurements have a 95% CI wider than 1 kcal/mol, and weighting by it uses every point in proportion to how much it is worth.",
